A||||5||Rodrv6||Aluminum cradle bushings from 1FST2M6||||14||
Z||000000||Rodrv6||09-04-2000||09:57 PM||||Dropped my Fiero off at 1FST2M6's house today.  This evening he brought it back to me complete with a set of the aluminum cradle bushings installed!  He even bled a little in the process. (I hate getting a finger where it shouldn't be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)  Took the car for a drive and here's what I think.<BR>First I'll list what the bushings do NOT do.<BR>No noise increase.<BR>No vibration increase.<BR>No adverse effects at all.<BR>Here's what they do.<BR>The car seems to be more solid feeling.  I took it around some corners fairly briskly and noticed that it is more stable, especially when the pavement is a little rough.  I'm sure the cradle was moving around a little before, and that would affect toe-in and camber.  Now it's restrained and the suspension has an easier time doing what it was designed to do.<BR>Would I do it again? You bet!  It was really nice to get them in and not get dirty!  Those of you who do not live 10 or 12 miles from 1FST2M6 will have to make your own arrangements <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||14
